@page "/docs/concepts/sso"
@layout DocsLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Single sign-on — Vaultex</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-eyebrow">Concepts</div>
<h1>Single sign-on</h1>
<p class="docs-lead">
    Once a user signs in to one app via Vaultex, they're signed in to every other app on the same
    Vaultex authority. Here's how that works and how to control it.
</p>

<h2 id="how">How SSO works</h2>
<p>
    When a user authenticates, Vaultex sets a session cookie on its own domain (<code>auth.vaultex.io</code>).
    The next time any client redirects to <code>/connect/authorize</code>, Vaultex sees the cookie,
    skips the login UI, and returns an authorization code immediately.
</p>
<p>
    This is intentional and correct. SSO is the whole reason customers adopt an identity provider.
    From the user's perspective, they sign in once per browser session and every subsequent app
    "just works."
</p>

<h2 id="prompt">Forcing re-authentication</h2>
<p>
    If you need to force a fresh sign-in (high-value transaction, step-up auth), pass
    <code>prompt=login</code> on the authorize request:
</p>

<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">URL</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>/connect/authorize?...&amp;prompt=login</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="logout">Single logout</h2>
<p>
    Calling <code>/connect/logout</code> ends the user's Vaultex session. They'll be prompted to
    sign in again the next time any app redirects to <code>/connect/authorize</code>.
</p>

<div class="docs-callout docs-callout--warn">
    <span class="docs-callout-icon">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M1 21h22L12 2 1 21zm12-3h-2v-2h2v2zm0-4h-2v-4h2v4z"/></svg>
    </span>
    <div class="docs-callout-body">
        <div class="docs-callout-title">App sessions are separate</div>
        <p>Logging out of Vaultex doesn't automatically clear your app's local session cookie. Your app should also clear its own session as part of its logout flow.</p>
    </div>
</div>

